// Overdrive line 4 ("Ignition") - granted once by IgnitionSkillAction.Execute, which SETs every field
// below to the picked rank's cumulative tuned values. All three ranks gate on being at max Rage
// (RageOverdriveUtility.IsAtMaxRage), not just Overdrive being active at all:
//  - Rank 1: BurnOnHitStacks toggles CharacterStats.BurnOnHitStacks on/off at the max-Rage threshold
//    (MaxAscensionUtility.OnEnteredMaxRage/RevertIgnition, same enter/exit-threshold shape Full
//    Throttle uses).
//  - Rank 2: HasBurningGround - a BURNING ENEMY KILLED while at max Rage leaves a burning-ground
//    patch where it died (MaxOverdriveReactionSystem.OnEntityKilled -> MaxAscensionUtility.
//    SpawnBurningGround). Reworked from an earlier distance-paced "drop a patch every N units
//    travelled" trail, which paid out regardless of whether Ignition's own Burn was doing anything.
//    Every knob the patch needs is authored here rather than baked into the prototype, so it can be
//    balanced without opening a prefab.
//  - Rank 3: HasInferno + InfernoRadius/InfernoBurnDuration/InfernoBurnIntensity back one
//    MaxAscensionUtility.ApplyRadialBurn pulse the FIRST time max Rage is reached each Overdrive
//    activation - InfernoTriggeredThisActivation latches that, reset by IgnitionSkillAction.Execute
//    on Begin.
component IgnitionUpgrade
{
    Byte BurnOnHitStacks;

    Boolean HasBurningGround;
    AssetRef<EntityPrototype> BurningGroundPrototype;
    FP BurningGroundDuration;
    FP BurningGroundRadius;
    FP BurningGroundDamage;
    FP BurningGroundTickInterval;

    Boolean HasInferno;
    FP InfernoRadius;
    FP InfernoBurnDuration;
    FP InfernoBurnIntensity;

    Boolean Applied;
    Boolean InfernoTriggeredThisActivation;
}
